#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ansel __is not__ a hobby project. It is a working tool designed to get job done, and\n"
"[the pact](./contribute/pact.md) commits it to responsibilities a hobby never carries.\n"
"Funding is your side of that pact: the project answers for your needs; its workers'\n"
"conditions are, in return, partly yours. What is the difference with a hobby project?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/donate.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chores"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Planning for long-term maintenance, stability and robustness implies doing chores, like\n"
"refactoring code, simplifying the programming structure, and identifying what features need\n"
"to be pruned. In addition of being tedious, these chores are often unpleasant, as they\n"
"don't involve any creativity and don't produce any cool new feature that will boost\n"
"marketing, but often require to understand some tangled and messy code written as someone\n"
"else's Saturday project.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's just boring responsible management, yet time-consuming. But someone needs to do it —\n"
"and it is precisely the work that never gets rewarded by applause, which is why it must be\n"
"rewarded by something else.\n"
msgstr ""

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Array Element: tags
#: content/donate.md:40
#: content/news/modules-groups-redesign/index.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Design"
msgstr "Design"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:45
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Design is what happens when you search for the simplest, minimalist, solution to somebody's\n"
"problem. Design requires the designer to understand the problem from the human perspective,\n"
"and to know the available technologies well enough to find out the most suited one.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The opposite of design is blindly \"adding support for …\", which implies you cram your\n"
"application with as many features as you can, until you can't maintain it anymore and you\n"
"move on to the next project. This is called\n"
"[feature creep](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feature_creep) and its effect on people is\n"
"called [feature fatigue](https://www.jstor.org/stable/30162393). It harms both projects and\n"
"people.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here again, the task is time-consuming, in addition of requiring a special set of skills\n"
"(_engineering_) that require time themselves to master. It goes way beyond the mere ability\n"
"to write code, most of it actually happens before any code is written, and when properly\n"
"done, it also reduces the amount of code needed, thus helping maintainability.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/donate.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overhead"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/donate.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The product is never the product, the product is always the service in which the product is\n"
"a key component. Delivering some software as an installable executable is not so hard.\n"
"Thinking that alone brings value to people is being deluded. Providing user support in a\n"
"timely manner, user education and debugging is the hardest part, as it is a recurring task\n"
"and a cognitive load, but that is required so users can actually get the job done.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: content/donate.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Responsible management"
msgstr ""

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
