#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "ansel via linux-on-ARM virtualization on macbook?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **koslowj** on 2024-11-04.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "The new M4 Macbooks look quite attractive, and apparently both windows 11 and linux-on-ARM can be virtualized either by using Parallels or UTM. Would it be feasible to run ansel in such a virtual machine, preferably under one of the several linux distributions supporting ARM (I'm not really interested in windows)? Emulation of x86 hardware may be too slow, even if my current desktop is rather slow anyway.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "I've already asked the developers of ansel on native Apple ARM hardware about the current status of their projects.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "**blankslatephoto** — 2024-12-02\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "This would be nice to have, both for \"optimized\" ARM platforms like the Mac, but for ARM in general; I like to do all of my developing on one software package, and right now I have to wait to get back to the laptop/desktop to produce jpegs, even for family photos (unless I want to just share what is in camera...). I played with compiling darktable a couple of years ago for ARM to no avail: with how fast the M4 and some snapdragon chips have become, perhaps basic edits can be completed in a linux VM... would be nice to have ansel on a tablet...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Has anyone tried compiling or running Ansel in a VM on something other than x86 recently?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "To answer the post: from your last posts, it looks like you have a need/want to run Ansel on ARM/Mac hardware: do you have access to an M4 (or the other ARM based macs?): might be easy to spin up a VM and see if the appimage will run and report back?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "It might not be that helpful (and I should do not while I should be working...), but I will try to spin up a VM in QEMU and see if the appimage runs (it should): don't know how helpful that will be, but if it is painfully slow or breaks while Fedora on a Ryzen 7 is under the VM, it might give us a data point...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "**koslowj** — 2024-12-02\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-via-linux-on-arm-virtualization-on.md:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thanks for your answer! I'm trying to decide whether to buy an M4 machine, but it has to be able to run ansel in some form or shape, either directly (some people have reported on that a while ago), or via Linux virtualization. Looking forward to your experimental results!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encouragement and how can I help?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **robbrown** on 2024-06-02.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "I'm watching this project with great interest. It is great to see a project and a small community try to move photography editing forward for open source. I never really got in to Darktable as it seemed too confusing and too bloated, especially since 4.0 and on. Already with the early work here on Ansel I see some great promise.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "My wishes for the project, and perhaps some good tenets:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- Prioritize user experience over features (for the sake of features). ie simple to understand and use the basics, with the ability to drill down to get more powerful editing options, if that is needed. Also an emphasis on good application speed as part of that experience.\n"
"- Good product lifecycle:\n"
"- think about the problem to solve first, design it correctly, engineer, test. Get feedback, and fine tune.\n"
"- be ok to deprecate old functionality / tools that could be better served by newer ones to avoid bloat and confusion\n"
"- keep experiments in a sandbox: Darktable 4+ is a classic case of sandboxing any and every idea in a production environment. In my experience, it is better to keep such experiments out of production, get the feedback and then move forward.... but only if the user experience is maintained.\n"
"- Good community & Tenets\n"
"- I've read some of the back story about Ansel and Darktable, and understand the frustrations with the latter project. It seems that Darktable had (or maybe steered away from) no tenets. I do hope that the Ansel project sticks to some solid tenets, which are regularly pointed to and considered when any change is made. In my professional experience developing and deploying complex systems good tenets allow a project to move in the right direction.\n"
msgstr ""

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:41
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Hope that helps.\n"
msgid "How can I help?\n"
msgstr "Hoffentlich hilft das.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"1.  While I'm not a developer, I'm a product manager and could perhaps help on this side of things.\n"
"2.  A simple act of \\$. I have set up a recurring payment, and hope others do too.\n"
msgstr ""

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:48
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Aurélien Pierre"
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2024-06-03\n"
msgstr "Aurélien Pierre"

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:50
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Thank you !\n"
msgid "Thanks and welcome !\n"
msgstr "Danke!\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "For now the focus is on improving core functionnalities :\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- making the picture import tool closer to a generic file picker (front-end is done but showed back-end issues, back-end has been rewritten and is almost ready for testing),\n"
"- making the pixelpipeline cache work properly so intermediate modules states can be stored instead of recomputed all the time (Darktable had an interesting way of solving cache consistency issues… by clearing the complete cache all the time),\n"
"- protecting the pictures from concurrent access throughout the app, but in an unified way (Darktable had 3 or 4 different thread-locks mechanisms to manage all corner cases).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/encouragement-and-how-can-i-help.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "So for now it's mostly code, and not the sexy kind.\n"
msgstr ""

