#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/some-usability-issues.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "While I haven't posted in a while, I've kept updating Ansel almost daily. I appreciate the amount of changes \"under the hood\", but certain usability features seem to have been lost, some of which actually worked quite well a while ago:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/some-usability-issues.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"- presently I cannot rotate gradient-masks; I can shift them, bend them, change their width, but rotation seems to be broken.\n"
"- retouching is (still) very difficult:\n"
"- -- I cannot use the brush, it produces a weird sequence of rectangles along a curve with no discernible effect;\n"
"- -- I cannot use the ellipse, as it's shape is fixed; while I can grow and shrink it, I cannot grab the horizontal resp. vertical extreme points to change its shape\n"
"- -- even circles and paths are hard to use, as it seems impossible to smoothly move the selected areas; they jump around uncontrollably;\n"
"- adjusting horizons or vertical lines has become difficult: when drawing a straight line that should be vertical or horizontal in the modified picture, an angle is displayed, but the resulting rotation is by a different angle which does not achieve the intended result. I have to remember the initial displayed angle and then rotate manually by that amount.\n"
"- the filmstrip no longer moves along and doesn't indicate the picture that's currently being worked on; if I have several similar pictures, I lose track of which one I'm working on.\n"
"- currently I cannot unfold grouped pictures; so it becomes very difficult to delete a whole group, as only the top picture is selected and then removed, leaving the rest of the group unaffected.\n"
"- adjusting the exposure correction by clicking on the pipette on the right makes dng-pictures way too dark (this is a long-standing problem, not quite as important as the ones above)\n"
msgstr ""

