msgid "Hi guys, I recently discovered Ansel as well as Darktable, got curious about Ansel because it claims to be faster than DT and I like the idea of it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "However on my windows 11 PC, Darktable feels faster while editing. In Ansel, I need to let go of the mouse for any edit to be displayed/updated, in DT the display is updated as I move the mouse, also, zooming in and out and navigating around the picture in DT has almost no lag as in Ansel I can't do it without getting a \"working\" message on the preview for a second or two.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is there anything I need to configure to make it better on windows? Is Linux where it's at?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:36
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lastly, is the option the move the histogram to the right gone right now? I saw in a user manual that such an option existed at some point.\n"
msgstr ""

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:42
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Aurélien Pierre"
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2024-07-29\n"
msgstr "Aurélien Pierre"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hi, there is a couple of things to precise here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ansel is faster than Darktable because many redundant operations, that computed more than once but which results were eventually discarded, were removed. Computing fewer things makes it objectively faster. Now, whether the speed-up will be noticeable or not on your particular hardware depends on how powerful it is, aka how much waste it can afford before feeling sluggish.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then we have responsiveness of the GUI, which is another (but related) layer on top: that's how fast the GUI gives you feedback that it got your input right.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "> In Ansel, I need to let go of the mouse for any edit to be displayed/updated\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is actually one of the methods used to limit intermediate useless recomputes. Darktable fires recomputations on \"button pushed\", \"button released\" and \"mouse moved\" events, without ensuring you are done interacting. That's fine on high-end hardware, but it can really lock your system on mid-range. Ansel only fires recomputations on \"button released\". The actual pipeline computations are the same in both applications.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "> Lastly, is the option the move the histogram to the right gone right now?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, the redesign of histogram is work in progress. Doc will follow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "**fourdogslong** — 2024-07-29\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thanks for your reply! Could an option to enable \"mouse moved\" be implemented in the future for those of us with capable hardware? I totally understand the reasoning behind it's removal but with a modern PC it feels weird / not natural to have to let go of the mouse to see a result. It makes precise adjustments harder in my opinion. Maybe ctrl+drag could be used to enable the \"mouse moved\" display refresh or something like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "I think I will try to install Linux anyway to see how it feels on that OS even though I am not familiar with the OS, it should be a fun experiement anyway. I was editing a picture in DarkTable yesterday, I'm still new to these Open Source software, and it crashed a few times using the color zones module, continuing the same edit in Ansel did not so I see the potential there.\n"
msgstr ""

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-performance-on-windows.md:66
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Thank you !\n"
msgid "Thanks for your work!\n"
msgstr "Danke!\n"

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
