#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "latest version 8de5c69 seg-faults here when compiled under Gentoo Linux 6.12.21; version dd6127b works fine"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:20
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here`.\n"
"No crawler ever captured this particular thread, so the text below — taken straight from the forum database — is the only copy left.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **koslowj** on 2025-04-15.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "I don't recall having seg-faults for a long time, but unfortunately, version 8de5c69 does so on my system. Fortunately I saved my previous version, which happened to be dd6127b, and it starts fine, even after recompiling it. Unfortunately, the file /tmp/ansel_bt_2MRV42.txt only contains the line \"this is ansel 8de5c69 reporting a segfault:\" and nothing else. The on-screen error messages start with\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[lib_load_module\\] failed to open \\`midi': /opt/ansel/lib64/ansel/plugins/lighttable/libmidi.so: undefined symbol: dt_register_input_driver\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[lib_load_module\\] failed to open \\`menu': /opt/ansel/lib64/ansel/plugins/lighttable/libmenu.so: undefined symbol: dt_ui_thumbtable\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\[lib_load_module\\] failed to open \\`filmstrip': libOpenEXR-3_2.so.31: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "and then go on for quite a while (which I can send, if required). Please advise how I can supply more meaningful error messages. What's also strange is that I cannot find dd6127b in the list of commits. We've been on vacation for a week and it cannot be much older than that. \\[I just noticed that I have openexr version 3.3.2-r1 installed.\\]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "**koslowj** — 2025-04-17\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "Concerning the mystery code number dd6127b: in the file build/CPackConfig.cmake in the source-tree that produces this version of ansel, the code d005a00 is mentioned instead. This indeed corresponds to a commit of about 2 weeks ago. I suppose that going through the subsequent patches one by one I should be able to find the one where things go wrong on my system, like looking for a bad Easter egg ;-)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "**koslowj** — 2025-04-18\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "The AppImage for 8de5c69 works fine, so the problem must be with the rest of my set-up :-(( Should have tried this earlier.\n"
msgstr ""

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/latest-version-8de5c69-seg-faults-here.md:53
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Aurélien Pierre"
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2025-04-18\n"
msgstr "Aurélien Pierre"

#. type: Plain text
