msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-crashes-during-start.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "After installation of Ansel on my Windows 11 laptop, when I start the program, it crashes after a minute or so : no UI appears at all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-crashes-during-start.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "I join here the trace file generated by Ansel. I think the problem is dealing with OpenCL functions...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-crashes-during-start.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note : The driver for my GPU (Intel IRIS Xe) is the latest one available (31.0.101).\n"
msgstr ""

# TRANSLATOR ChatGPT
#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-crashes-during-start.md:37
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "Aurélien Pierre"
msgid "**Aurélien Pierre** — 2023-04-20\n"
msgstr "Aurélien Pierre"

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-crashes-during-start.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "You have an OpenCL error here, probably linked to a rotten OpenCL/GPU driver. Try to update/downgrade that driver or remove it entirely. Alternatively, you can try to start Ansel in command line with `--disable-opencl`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/ansel-crashes-during-start.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that running the latest driver is not always the best idea, if you use experimental branches. Try to stick to the stable/production drivers, which are never the latest.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#: content/community/windows-7.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Windows 7"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:21
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The original address was `https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/windows-7`.\n"
"You can check this copy against the [snapshot in the Internet Archive](https://web.archive.org/web/20230601123252/https://community.ansel.photos/view-discussion/windows-7).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Posted by **Vintage Lens Lover** on 2023-03-24.*\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the excitement of discovering Ansel I was pretty gutted to see the Windows download was for Windows 10 and 11 only. Despite of this I thought I'd download the installer and see if it would work on Windows 7 and to my pleasant surprise it does!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is there any reason Windows 7 compatibility should break in the future?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, I am bitterly clinging onto Windows 7 for games and Affinity Photo until I figure out how to get all that running on Linux too. Having Affinity Photo and Ansel on different boot drives would be far from ideal.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Windows download is marked for 10 and 11 because I know it works on these. Not knowing if it does on 7, I will make no promise that I can't keep.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "I'm glad to hear it works on 7 too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "As with any software relying on 3rd-party libraries, the challenge is rather to ensure each and every one of them keeps working on platform XYZ. The most potential I see for breakage is from Gtk, which behaves already unreliably on Windows in some contexts, and as many FLOSS projects, lacks dev and beta-testers on Windows.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Vintage Lens Lover** — 2023-03-24\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fair enough and thank you for the reply!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:52
#, no-wrap
msgid "I'll have to figure out how to install it on Linux (and how to get Affinity Photo ported too). I know there were some people who made progress on porting AF using WINE but it looked complicated.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:54
#, no-wrap
msgid "P.S. - Your rant on DT4 was highly amusing. Well done putting together Ansel! I only installed it last night, it's taking a little getting used to but so far it does actually feel a little faster.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "**ariznaf** — 2023-03-28\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "I have not tried, but It is quite probable that It world with no problema.in Windows 7.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "It all depends on having a display driver forbyourbgpu with OpenGL 1.2 support in orden to have GPU support.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "But you can allways use the CPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "DT does not seem ti use OS advance features or new libraries o technologies, but the GPU.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Vintage Lens Lover** — 2023-03-28\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:72
#, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, it IS working fine in Windows 7 so far.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:74
#, no-wrap
msgid "Windows 10 was always a line in the sand for me so I've been migrating to Linux over the last two to three years (wish I'd done it sooner).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coming from DT 4.2.1 a few of the modules complained when importing from XMP: Highlight Reconstruction, Filmic and I think Lens Correction were not happy. I had Highlight Reconstruction set to \"inpaint opposed\" in DT and had to select a new option in Ansel.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:80
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Vintage Lens Lover** — 2025-01-09\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "I don't really expect it to be fixed, but the more recent builds of Ansel throw up an error in Windows 7 now. [ansel-43e4fce-win64.exe](https://github.com/aurelienpierreeng/ansel/releases/download/v0.0.0/ansel-43e4fce-win64.exe) seems to be the latest version to successfully launch in Windows 7, in case anyone else was dealing with the same issue.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:88
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can you be more specific on the error ?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "I suppose the most probable cause for this Windows the building environment (MSYS2, MingW64, URTC64, etc.) that got updated to something incompatible.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thanks for the response. A box pops up which says:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:98
#, no-wrap
msgid "\"ansel.exe - Entry Point Not Found\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/windows-7.md:100
#, no-wrap
msgid "The procedure entry point CreateFile2 could not be located in the dynamic link library KERNEL32.dll.\"\n"
msgstr ""

