#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/image-upload-improvements.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "While this solution works well enough I think this feature can be better than just the piwigo api. I would like to also send the sidecar file and raw files to my album solution since it can also present that as optional downloads with the pictures alongside the metadata. Also it does not support uploading pictures that are not part of an album so I'd have to make a dummy album to just upload single pictures.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/image-upload-improvements.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "There's way more album hosting solutions than mine so maybe it makes sense to make a slightly more generic and way better documented API to support uploading images?\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/image-upload-improvements.md:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload to web services typically use Rest API and each API is slightly different on server end, so I am not confident that we could have one unified client API to handle them all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/image-upload-improvements.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "The now-defunct Flickr API used to use the key/wallet service of the OS (Gnome Keyring or KDE Wallet), I think the lack of support for them in Piwigo is just developer's lazyness. Problem remains that these are not avalaible outside of Linux anyway, so portability is a concern here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/image-upload-improvements.md:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "**MartijnBraam** — 2023-03-23\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: content/community/image-upload-improvements.md:47
