#. type: Plain text
#: content/contribute/design.md:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "Discussions close. When the same arguments start repeating, the decision is made with what is known, recorded with its reasons, and the thread is closed — a decision debated forever is a decision made by fatigue. The counterpart of closing is reversibility: a decision stands until real use proves it wrong, and evidence reopens what repetition cannot. If validation later shows the adopted solution fails its own acceptance criteria, it goes back to this stage — the [sunk cost](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunk_cost) of the prototype buys it nothing.\n"
msgstr ""

